    description: "WHAT (as reported)\nThe size-limited JSON spends most of its budget on metadata (Flask):\n- survey.4k.json holds 9 symbols; about 70% of it is profile, reproducibility_context and similar.\n- survey --compact, which the README calls the LLM-friendly JSON, is about 72k tokens for 100 symbols; 34 of them come from examples/, and 19% of the file is run logs.\nThe reviewer's comparison: the 4k Markdown sketch conveyed far more. The budgets themselves were met (3,911 / 15,834 / 63,925 tokens).\nAlso reported: the full survey is 11.2 MB for about 26,000 lines of Flask (average node 1.1 KB, edge 0.6 KB), about 900 of 3,656 nodes from .rst directives.\n\nREPORTED, NOT RE-RUN. Source: an outside reviewer who tried hypergumbo 10.0.0 from PyPI on 2026-11-24 (transcript pasted by the owner in session). Nothing in this item was run on dev by the filing agent unless a line says so; the reviewer's fixtures are not on this machine. FIRST STEP: reproduce on current dev with a fixture, and check the unreleased changelog, before building anything. Filed at the owner's request (\"file them all now\")."  # d8a0
